WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:04.605
Ten teams copy the same twelve files and change three lines.

2
00:00:04.625 --> 00:00:07.490
Then one fix must be made in ten places.

3
00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:12.565
This port has three steps: use a chart, write a chart, and choose your tool.

4
00:00:12.585 --> 00:00:15.125
First: a package for Kubernetes.

5
00:00:15.145 --> 00:00:17.475
A chart is a set of templates with a version.

6
00:00:17.495 --> 00:00:19.535
Values fill the blanks.

7
00:00:19.555 --> 00:00:21.298
Each install is a release.

8
00:00:21.318 --> 00:00:23.645
Helm keeps every revision of it.

9
00:00:23.665 --> 00:00:27.470
So an upgrade that goes wrong is one rollback away.

10
00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.205
Second: write one chart for all teams.

11
00:00:30.225 --> 00:00:32.317
Put good defaults in the values file.

12
00:00:32.337 --> 00:00:34.940
Each team changes only what differs.

13
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.803
Render the chart before you install it.

14
00:00:36.823 --> 00:00:38.865
Read the output.

15
00:00:38.885 --> 00:00:40.950
Third: which tool, and when?

16
00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:42.963
Helm packages software for others.

17
00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:46.025
Kustomize patches your own files.

18
00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:47.860
Quick recap of Helm.

19
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.048
A chart is templates plus values.

20
00:00:50.068 --> 00:00:51.685
A release has revisions.

21
00:00:51.705 --> 00:00:53.820
Render before you install.

22
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.940
Now start the first lesson below.
